join Charity (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Charity: I have been at this eleven years through the district. I am going to stop.
- Stop asking?
	Hope: Stop asking?
	Charity: Stop asking THEM. The ward puts it in the plan, the plan goes to the district, the district does not get the allocation, and the following year we start again.
	Charity: There are organisations that fund boreholes directly. I know how to write to them. I have known how for six years.
	- Then why haven't you?
		Hope: Then why haven't you?
		Charity: Because it is not my village.
		Charity: If I petition an NGO and it fails, this village has been through it twice and will not try a third time. That is not a decision I get to make on my own.
Charity: There is a discussion at the Gathering Tree on Thursday. It was called before I decided anything — people have been talking about the water for weeks.
- What do you need from me?
	Hope: What do you need from me?
	Charity: Be there. Listen to what people actually say rather than what I hope they say.
	Charity: And watch Gogo. If she is behind it, the village is behind it, and I will spend the next month writing. If she is not, I will not, and that will be the correct outcome.
	- Should I talk to her first?
		Hope: Should I talk to her first?
		Charity: No.
		Charity: If she says yes because a friend asked her to, it is worth nothing. It has to be the room.
		Charity: Thursday. Just come.
set {GameState.quest_village_borehole_conversation_main} = "active"
[signal arg="objective:Attend the discussion at the Gathering Tree"]
[signal arg="hearts:charity:1"]
